# parse/const (id 76): constant entry around the number lexer. RDOK = 0 in PC 1 or 2 fetches char I.
# PC 1 prefix: space or '+' skip, '-' NEG, '(' NEG and PAR, '$' skip, digit -> lnum PC 1 (re-read),
#   '.' -> lnum PC 2, anything else or end -> ckey (77) from char 0.
# PC 2 suffix (after lnum): '%' once, ')' if PAR, spaces, end -> numconv (FRAC += 2 PCT, return 76 PC 3),
#   else -> PC 5 (text).
# PC 3: number result (TK 11 = out of range -> text). PC 5: plain text A = (2, HS). PC 6: apostrophe text
#   from lstr: write HEAP_TOP, A = (2, TV). PC 3, 5, 6 exit through restore (79).
# Note: weights/parse/const.md
